            {
                "entry_id": "4f5b432e-8964-3e0b-9ee8-dde2638778fe",
                "word": "wold",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "63c67b1a-8db2-46fa-a7cd-660382d28037",
                        "entry_id": "4f5b432e-8964-3e0b-9ee8-dde2638778fe",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "wolds"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                        "entry_id": "4f5b432e-8964-3e0b-9ee8-dde2638778fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An unforested or deforested plain, a grassland, a moor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "regional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0da31224-0d19-487d-8058-c1c830fe5986",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "Saint Withold footed thrice the ’old;\nHe met the nightmare, and her nine fold;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "163494e1-e244-4657-994a-4a386bca5aea",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "[…]—I came with my cousin, Frank Osbaldistone, there, and I must shew him the way back again to the Hall, or he’ll lose himself in the wolds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17d94951-bfbf-4cca-a330-f6f7627b1f8b",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "And therefore did he take a trusty band\nTo traverse Acarnania forest wide,\nIn war well-seasoned, and with labours tanned,\nTill he did greet white Achelous’ tide,\nAnd from his farther bank Ætolia’s wolds espied."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "694d64ad-8685-44d1-9784-8c1d94a19ccd",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "The wind that beats the mountain, blows\nMore softly round the open wold,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b64d622f-eabf-49d9-925c-062761c0cdfb",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "Blossomed the opening spring, and the notes of the robin and bluebird\nSounded sweet upon wold and in wood, yet Gabriel came not."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d1b8e8f-4fad-4edd-85b8-413a1a23ac11",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "Take counsel, sever from my lot your lot,\nDwell in your pleasant places, hoard your gold;\nLest you with me should shiver on the wold,\nAthirst and hungering on a barren spot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b71bd84-e666-44f3-8c59-471a19f1b70c",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "Before yon field of trembling gold\nIs garnered into dusty sheaves,\nOr ere the autumn’s scarlet leaves\nFlutter as birds adown the wold,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f2eb1d7-342c-423f-9890-ddc71ee27643",
                                "sense_id": "e941fc12-1edb-3a27-89e1-c9fdc6956482",
                                "text": "It seemed to be a fairly large and prosperous farm, grouped round a modest country house standing among trees as shelter from the wind. About it rolled the open pasture of the wold, as far as could be seen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6a9719d1-3aa3-3dff-9563-a376ccefd90c",
                        "entry_id": "4f5b432e-8964-3e0b-9ee8-dde2638778fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A wood or forest, especially a wooded upland."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
